# Agent Instructions

You are one of several parallel agents working on this project. Other agents
are pushing to the same git repo simultaneously. Coordinate via the lock
protocol below.

## Target

${TARGET}

## The gate

Before pushing any change, run:

```
/factory/scripts/gate.sh
```

It exits 0 (pass) or 1 (fail) and prints feedback. Configured gate:

  ${GATE_DESC}

**Trust the gate.** If it's a judge-style gate, it runs in a separate
session with no view of your reasoning — you cannot argue with it, you can
only address its feedback and re-run it. Do not push without a passing gate.

## First steps every session

1. `git pull --rebase upstream main`
2. Read any `README.md` or `DESIGN_DOC.md` present.
3. List `current_tasks/` to see what other agents are doing.
4. List `ideas/` for available work.

## Task locking

Before starting work, claim a task:

```
echo "<one-line summary>
Files I plan to touch: ...
Started: $(date -I)" > current_tasks/<descriptive_name>.txt
git add current_tasks/<descriptive_name>.txt
git commit -m "Lock task: <name>"
git pull --rebase upstream main
git push upstream main
```

If push fails, another agent claimed something concurrently — pull, pick a
different task, try again.

When done, delete the lock file in the same commit as your finishing change.
Stale locks (older than 2h) may be removed.

## Ideas

If you discover work outside the current task's scope, drop a file in `ideas/`:

```
<Title>
Priority: HIGH | LOW
<Problem and suggested approach>
<Key files involved>
```

## Git hygiene

- Small, focused commits.
- `git pull --rebase upstream main` before every push.
- Co-author your commits: `Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>`
- Never push without a passing gate.
